UID:submission-cce3a147fd9a8d2e@norwood.ma
DTSTAMP:20260926T183700Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T150000
SUMMARY:Day House Tour
LOCATION:Norwood Historical Society — 93 Day Street
DESCRIPTION:Step into history with a guided tour of the F. Holland Day House\, a stunning Victorian home nestled in Norwood\, Massachusetts. Visitors can explore the beautifully preserved rooms\, admire period furnishings\, and learn about Day's contributions to the arts and literature. The house itself\, built in 1859\, stands as a testament to 19th-century architecture and the cultural richness of the era. We are excited to also share a new exhibit at the Day House\, 1776 - What Survives. The focus is on Norwood\nCost: Free\, donation appreciated\nSource: https://norwoodhistoricalsociety.org/events/
URL:https://norwoodhistoricalsociety.org/events/
END:VEVENT
